    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0709" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13822: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-09T11:00:00+03:00">August 9, 1941—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1457. For the President, the Secretary and the Under Secretary. I have sent the
                    following telegram to Harry Hopkins in care of our Embassy in London: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“For Harry Hopkins from the Ambassador:</p>
                        <p>The Chinese Ambassador today called on me to deliver an official
                            invitation to you from Generalissimo Chiang Kai Shek and Vice President
                            H. H. Kung to visit Chungking. The invitation, which is in the <pb
                                facs="0710" n="700" xml:id="pg700"/> form of a cablegram dated
                            August 5 from Chungking to the Ambassador, reads as follows: <quote
                                rend="blockquote">
                                <p>‘To Mr. Harry Hopkins. On behalf of the Chinese Government we
                                    send you hearty greetings and a cordial invitation to visit
                                    Chungking on your way back to the United States. We hope that
                                    you may find it possible to do so. Chiang Kai Shek, H. H.
                                    Kung.’</p>
                            </quote>
                        </p>
                        <p>“I have informed the Chinese Ambassador of your return to London and that
                            the invitation is being transmitted to you telegraphically. Kind
                            regards.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
